{
  "abstract": "A complete, elementary Lean 4 proof that every convex set in R^3 has additive VC_2-dimension at most 2, settling the open conjecture VCDimConvex.hasAddVCNDimAtMost_two_two_of_convex_r3 from Google DeepMind's Formal Conjectures repository. Combined with Kenta Kitamura's 2x2 lower bound, this determines the exact value VC_2(convex sets in R^3) = 2 (improving the previous finite upper bound of 2^128 - 1). The proof uses no topology, no Hahn-Banach theorem, and no closedness assumptions on C: it shows no coplanar 2x3 grid is in convex position, reduces any non-degenerate 3x3 grid via an explicit invertible affine map to paraboloid normal form, and derives a 4-point convex combination contradiction from just two 7-point masks.",
